---
/**
 * TODO(client): accurate to how the site now works — brands email, creators
 * apply through the form on /become-a-creator/, which saves each application
 * to a Google Sheet, with a backup copy in Netlify Forms.
 * A published policy still needs the registered legal entity, its address and
 * a decision on naming a Data Protection Officer (marked inline). Have it
 * reviewed before launch: AMAVI holds personal data on EU creators and brands,
 * so GDPR applies.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME, CREATOR_PATH, REGION } from '../consts';

const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How AMAVI Socials collects, uses and stores personal data from brands and creators, and the rights you have under GDPR."
>
  <section class="section page-head">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1 class="display display--lg">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta page-head__meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="policy">
        <p class="policy__lead">
          This policy explains what personal data {SITE_NAME} collects, why, how long we
          keep it, and what you can ask us to do with it. It covers brands who email us
          and creators who apply to join our network through the application form on this
          site.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} is a creator-led marketing and partnerships agency working with brands across {REGION}. For the
          purposes of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) we are the data
          controller for the information described below.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): insert the registered legal entity name, company registration
          number and registered address. A published policy needs all three.]
        </p>
        <p>
          You can reach us about anything in this policy at
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>

        <h3>If you email us as a brand</h3>
        <p>
          When you email us we receive your name, your email address and whatever you
          include in your message, typically your company, what you want to achieve and a
          rough budget.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this solely to reply and to discuss working together. Our lawful basis is
          our legitimate interest in responding to an enquiry you started. We do not add
          enquiry contacts to a mailing list.
        </p>

        <h3>If you apply to join the creator network</h3>
        <p>
          Through our <a href={CREATOR_PATH}>creator application form</a> we collect
          your name, email address, location, links to your social channels, your follower
          range, your engagement rate, your niches, your collaboration preferences, the
          content formats you produce, your rates, any audience insights you choose to
          share, past brand collaborations, a media kit link, and any other notes you add.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this to maintain our creator database and to match creators to client
          briefs. <strong>We share these details with our clients</strong> when we are
          considering you for a collaboration. That is the purpose of the database, and
          it is what the consent checkbox on the form covers. Our lawful basis is your
          consent.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Brand enquiries are kept for as long as we are in active conversation with you,
          and for a reasonable period afterwards in case the conversation resumes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Creator details are kept in our database until you ask us to remove them. We do
          not set an automatic expiry, because the value of the database to you is that
          we can come to you when something fits, potentially years after you sign up.
          You can ask us to delete your details at any time.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): if you want a fixed retention period instead, for example
          reviewing creator records every 24 months, state it here.]
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Our clients.</strong> Creator details are shared with the brands we
            represent, for the purpose of considering you for collaborations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Workspace.</strong> Handles our email, so brand enquiries are
            stored there, holds the spreadsheet creator applications are saved to, and
            receives a copy of each application by email when it arrives.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Netlify.</strong> Hosts this website and keeps a backup copy of each
            creator application through Netlify Forms. Like any web host it also processes
            standard request logs, such as IP addresses, to serve pages.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): confirm the applications spreadsheet, and the mailbox the
          notification emails go to, live in AMAVI’s Google Workspace account rather than
          a personal Google account, and name any further tool applications are moved on
          to, such as a database or CRM, here too.]
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it with anyone else for their
          own marketing purposes.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): if an analytics tool, CRM or email platform is added, list it
          here. If a tool transfers data outside the EEA, that transfer and its safeguard
          must be named.]
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site sets no cookies of its own and uses no advertising or tracking
          cookies. Because nothing non-essential is set, no cookie banner is shown.
        </p>
        <p class="policy__todo">
          [TODO(client): analytics has not been added yet. If GA4 is chosen it sets
          cookies and a consent banner becomes legally required before it loads. A
          cookieless tool such as Plausible would not change this section.]
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
          <li>ask us to correct anything inaccurate;</li>
          <li>ask us to delete your data;</li>
          <li>ask us to restrict how we use it;</li>
          <li>ask us to transfer it to you or another provider;</li>
          <li>object to our use of it; and</li>
          <li>
            withdraw your consent at any time, which stops any further use without
            affecting what was lawful beforehand.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these, email
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We will respond within
          one month.
        </p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe we have handled your data improperly, you can complain to the
          Irish Data Protection Commission at
          <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dataprotection.ie</a>.
          We would rather you came to us first so we can put it right.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how we handle personal data we will update this page and change
          the date at the top.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .page-head__meta { margin-top: var(--space-s); }

  .policy { max-width: var(--measure); }

  .policy__lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: 1.45;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-l);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-stretch: var(--display-stretch);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: var(--display-sm);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .policy h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--weight-strong);
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  /* Body copy stays at the regular weight: this page is read, not skimmed. */
  .policy p + p { margin-top: var(--space-s); }

  .policy ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }
  .policy li {
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    position: relative;
  }
  .policy li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0; top: 0.8em;
    width: 0.5em;
    border-top: var(--stroke) solid var(--line);
  }

  /* Visible on purpose: these are unresolved and must not ship unnoticed.
     A black outline and heavier type mark them, not a colour. */
  .policy__todo {
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
    padding: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
    border: var(--stroke) solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-strong);
  }
</style>
